  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Task 2: free-parameter rotation families on <0|",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 2(a): the one-site kappa-families on the SoV vacuum <0| (g = 1), explicit group elements, exact identities and overlap identities.\n   o_s = O_s / lambda_s:  <0|o_s = <0|rho_s(gamma^{p_s}),  O = (X, Y, Z, W) = (t1(th1)^-1, t1(th2), t1(th3), t1(th4)^-1),  p = (1, 1, -1, -1), gamma = G^-T.\n   Site vector after (1 - kappa_s o_s):  v_s = vac_s (1 - kappa_s rho_s(gamma^{p_s})). *)\nn0 = Length[checks]; $wp = 60;\nkap = Symbol[\"kap\"];\nq1c1 = q1cl c1cl;     (* <0|t3(theta1 - h) = q1 c1 <0|rho_1(gamma) *)\nt3cov = covW[OmC, {tD[3, thL4[[1]] - hN]}];\nv1k = Flatten[KroneckerProduct[e1v . (id4 - kap gam), e4v, e1v, e4v]];\nchecks[\"(a) <0|t3(th1-h) = q1 c1 <0|rho_1(gamma) (exact), q1 c1 = detG (-6h^3) (th12-h)(th12-2h)(th12-4h)(th13-h)(th13-2h)(th13-3h)(th14-h)(th14-2h)(th14-4h)\"] = t3cov === q1c1 Flatten[KroneckerProduct[e1v . gam, e4v, e1v, e4v]];\nchecks[\"(a) <0|(1 - kappa t3(th1-h)/(q1 c1)) = e1^T (1 - kappa G^-T) (x) e4^T (x) e1^T (x) e4^T (exact, kappa symbolic)\"] = Simplify[OmC - kap t3cov/q1c1 - v1k] === ConstantArray[0, 256];\nchecks[\"explicit site vectors from the companion matrix: e1^T G^-T = -e4^T/c4, e4^T G = e3^T, e1^T G^T = (c1, 1, 0, 0), e4^T G^-1 = (-1, c1, -c2, c3)/c4  (c_k = e_k(z))\"] = {e1v . gam === -e4v/cc[[4]], e4v . GcN === UnitVector[4, 3], e1v . Transpose[GcN] === {cc[[1]], 1, 0, 0}, e4v . Inverse[GcN] === {-1, cc[[1]], -cc[[2]], cc[[3]]}/cc[[4]]};\n(* overlaps with all 256 twisted eigenkets (companion frame Psi = R Psi_diag), numeric 60 digits *)\nRfrN = N[Rfr, $wp];\novlOf[w_] := N[w, $wp] . RfrN . rAll;          (* <w|Psi_n> for every eigenket, companion-frame covector w *)\nov0 = ovlOf[OmC];\nchecks[\"<0|Psi_n> != 0 for all 256 eigenkets (min |<0|Psi_n>| over n, rAll normalised as eigh output)\"] = N[Min[Abs[ov0]], 5];\ntauO = <|1 -> 1/tauVec[1, thL4[[1]]], 2 -> tauVec[1, thL4[[2]]], 3 -> tauVec[1, thL4[[3]]], 4 -> 1/tauVec[1, thL4[[4]]]|>;   (* eigenvalues of X, Y, Z, W *)\nchecks[\"tau_3(th1-h) tau_1(th1) = q1 on every eigenket (max rel dev)\"] = N[Max[Abs[tauVec[3, thL4[[1]] - hN] tauVec[1, thL4[[1]]]/q1cl - 1]], 3];\nkapN = 3/7;\nsiteVec[s_, k_] := Flatten[KroneckerProduct @@ Table[If[r == s, vacOf1[r] . (id4 - k siteMat[chainData[\"L4\"][\"reps\"][[r]], MatrixPower[gam, pS[r]]]), vacOf1[r]], {r, 4}]];\nvacOf1[r_] := If[chainData[\"L4\"][\"reps\"][[r]] === rhoA, e1v, e4v];\novDev = Table[Max[Abs[ovlOf[siteVec[s, kapN]] - (1 - kapN tauO[s]/lamS[s]) ov0]/Abs[ov0]], {s, 4}];\nchecks[\"overlap identity <0|(1 - kappa o_s)|Psi_n> = (1 - kappa tau_{O_s}/lambda_s) <0|Psi_n> for s = 1..4 (kappa = 3/7), max rel dev over 256 eigenkets\"] = N[ovDev, 3];\n(* the group elements: site s of the family carries (1 - kappa_s gamma^{p_s}) as a matrix acting on the covector (the rho_F-element is its inverse transpose) *)\ngrpEl[s_, k_] := If[chainData[\"L4\"][\"reps\"][[s]] === rhoA, id4 - k MatrixPower[gam, pS[s]], Transpose[Inverse[id4 - k Transpose[Inverse[MatrixPower[gam, pS[s]]]]]]];\nchecks[\"group element on each site: h_1 = 1 - kappa G^-T; h_2 = (1 - kappa G)^-T; h_3 = 1 - kappa G^T; h_4 = (1 - kappa G^-1)^-T.  rho_s(h_s) reproduces the site vector (exact check at kappa = 3/7)\"] = And @@ Table[vacOf1[s] . siteMat[chainData[\"L4\"][\"reps\"][[s]], grpEl[s, kapN]] === vacOf1[s] . (id4 - kapN siteMat[chainData[\"L4\"][\"reps\"][[s]], MatrixPower[gam, pS[s]]]), {s, 4}];\nGrid[Transpose[{Keys[checks][[n0 + 1 ;;]], Values[checks][[n0 + 1 ;;]]}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Results, cell 25:** **(a) the kappa-family [exact, kappa symbolic]:** <0|t3(theta1-h) = q1 c1 <0|rho_1(gamma) and **<0|(1 - kappa t3(theta1-h)/(q1 c1)) = e1^T (1 - kappa G^-T) (x) e4^T (x) e1^T (x) e4^T**, with q1 c1 the closed form above. Explicit site vectors from the companion matrix (exact): e1^T G^-T = -e4^T/E4, e4^T G = e3^T, e1^T G^T = (E1, 1, 0, 0), e4^T G^-1 = (-1, E1, -E2, E3)/E4, so v1(k) = (1, 0, 0, k/E4), v2(k) = (0, 0, -k, 1), v3(k) = (1 - k E1, -k, 0, 0), v4(k) = (k/E4, -k E1/E4, k E2/E4, 1 - k E3/E4). **Group elements:** h1 = 1 - k G^-T, h2 = (1 - k G)^-T, h3 = 1 - k G^T, h4 = (1 - k G^-1)^-T, with rho_A(h) = h, rho_F(h) = h^-T (exact check). **Overlap identity on all 256 eigenkets [numeric 60 digits]:** <0|(1 - kappa o_s)|Psi> = (1 - kappa ohat_s) <0|Psi> with o_s = O_s/lambda_s and ohat_s its eigenvalue, max rel dev 10^-51 (s = 1..4); **ohat_1 = h th12 (th13+h) th14/tau_1(th1) = tau_3(th1-h)/(q1 c1)**, ohat_2 = tau_1(th2)/(h th12 th23 (th24-h)), ohat_3 = tau_1(th3)/(h th32 (th31+h) th34), ohat_4 = -h th43 (th42-h) th41/tau_1(th4). The operator identity tau_3(th1-h) tau_1(th1) = q1 holds on every eigenket (10^-47). <0|Psi_n> != 0 for all 256 eigenstates (min 6.2e-4), i.e. <0| is cyclic for the Bethe algebra.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 2(b)-(c): which products of single-site kappa-deformations are polynomials in the Bethe-algebra words?\n   P_e = (x)_s [vac_s rho_s(gamma^{p_s})^{e_s}] (pure rotated products), words <0|o_e = <0| prod_{s in e} o_s with o_s = O_s/lambda_s (16 words).\n   Every P_e is expressed in the span of the 16 words by an exact linear solve; the site sets S for which ALL P_e with support in S lie in the span are\n   those for which (x)_{s in S}(1 - kappa_s ...) is an explicit polynomial in the commuting o_s. *)\nn0 = Length[checks];\nsubsE = Tuples[{0, 1}, 4];\nbits[e_] := StringJoin[ToString /@ e];\nwordsO = Table[covW[OmC, opS /@ Select[Range[4], e[[#]] == 1 &]]/(Times @@ Table[If[e[[s]] == 1, lamS[s], 1], {s, 4}]), {e, subsE}];   (* <0| o_e *)\nprodsP = Table[Flatten[KroneckerProduct @@ Table[facS[s, e[[s]]], {s, 4}]], {e, subsE}];                                              (* P_e *)\nchecks[\"rank of the 16 words <0|o_e, of the 16 products P_e, of both together\"] = {MatrixRank[wordsO], MatrixRank[prodsP], MatrixRank[Join[wordsO, prodsP]]};\nMsol = Table[Quiet[Check[LinearSolve[Transpose[wordsO], prodsP[[i]]], $Failed]], {i, 16}];\ninSpan = (# =!= $Failed &) /@ Msol;\nchecks[\"P_e in the span of the 16 words? (e as bit string over sites 1234)\"] = Table[bits[subsE[[i]]] -> inSpan[[i]], {i, 16}];\nokSets = Select[Rest[Subsets[Range[4]]], Function[S, AllTrue[Range[16], Function[i, Or[AnyTrue[Range[4], subsE[[i, #]] == 1 && ! MemberQ[S, #] &], inSpan[[i]]]]]]];\nmaxSets = Select[okSets, Function[S, ! AnyTrue[okSets, Function[S2, S2 =!= S && SubsetQ[S2, S]]]]];\nchecks[\"site sets S such that every product deformation on S is a polynomial in the o_s: maximal sets\"] = maxSets;\nchecks[\"P_e = sum_e' N_{e e'} <0|o_e' : the non-diagonal expansions (e -> {e' -> coefficient}), exact\"] = Table[bits[subsE[[i]]] -> (Table[bits[subsE[[j]]] -> Msol[[i, j]], {j, Flatten[Position[Msol[[i]], x_ /; x =!= 0, {1}, Heads -> False]]}]), {i, Select[Range[16], inSpan[[#]] && Count[Msol[[#]], x_ /; x =!= 0] > 1 &]}];\n(* interference term for the failing products: structure of P_e - (projection on the words) in the sites {1,4} pair *)\nTc[c_] := Flatten[MatrixPower[GcN, c]];                         (* <S_14| rho_4(gamma^c) as a vector on sites (1,4): sum_i e_i (x) e_i G^c *)\nfail = Select[Range[16], ! inSpan[[#]] &];\nextraVecs[c_] := Flatten[Table[Flatten[Transpose[ArrayReshape[Flatten[KroneckerProduct[Tc[c], f2, f3]], {4, 4, 4, 4}], {1, 4, 2, 3}]], {f2, {vacOf1[2], vacOf1[2] . siteMat[rhoF, gam]}}, {f3, {vacOf1[3], vacOf1[3] . siteMat[rhoA, MatrixPower[gam, -1]]}}], 1];\nrk = Table[{c, MatrixRank[Join[wordsO, extraVecs[c]]], And @@ Table[MatrixRank[Append[Join[wordsO, extraVecs[c]], prodsP[[i]]]] == MatrixRank[Join[wordsO, extraVecs[c]]], {i, fail}]}, {c, -3, 3}];\nchecks[\"adding the 4 singlet-channel covectors <S_14|rho_4(gamma^c) (x) {vac_2, vac_2 gamma} (x) {vac_3, vac_3 gamma^-1} to the words: {c, rank, all failing P_e then in the span?}\"] = rk;\nGrid[Transpose[{Keys[checks][[n0 + 1 ;;]], Values[checks][[n0 + 1 ;;]]}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Results, cell 27 (exact):** the 16 words <0|o_e (o_s = O_s/lambda_s, e in {0,1}^4) have rank 16, the 16 pure rotated products P_e = (x)_s [vac_s rho_s(gamma^p_s)^e_s] have rank 16, together rank 20: the spans differ. **P_e lies in the span of the words for all e except e = 1001, 1011, 1101, 1111** (the products that rotate BOTH end sites). The site sets S for which every product deformation (x)_{s in S}(1 - kappa_s ..) is an explicit polynomial in the o_s are the maximal sets **{1,2,3} and {2,3,4}** (three consecutive sites; larger word pools are tested in cell 33). **Exchange expansions (exact):** P_0101 = (20/31) o_0000 + (11/31) o_0101, P_0111 = (20/31) o_0010 + (11/31) o_0111, P_1010 = -(77/68) o_0000 + (145/68) o_1010, P_1110 = -(77/68) o_0100 + (145/68) o_1110, i.e. with the numbers h/th24 = 20/31, (th24-h)/th24 = 11/31, h/th13 = -77/68, (th13-h)/th13 = 145/68 (closed forms verified in 29). **Adding the four singlet-channel covectors <S_14|rho_4(gamma^c) (x) {vac_2, vac_2 gamma} (x) {vac_3, vac_3 gamma^-1} to the words (rank 20) puts the four failing products in the span exactly for c = -1** (not for the other c = -3..3).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 2(b)-(c) continued: closed-form expansions of the product deformations, the overlap polynomials on the reachable site sets {1,2,3}, {2,3,4},\n   and the interference term for the two end sites. Notation: o_s = O_s/lambda_s, ohat_s = eigenvalue of o_s = tauO[s]/lamS[s], P_e pure rotated products, v_s(kappa) = vac_s (1 - kappa rho_s(gamma^{p_s})). *)\nn0 = Length[checks]; $wp = 60;\noword[ss_List] := covW[OmC, opS /@ ss]/(Times @@ (lamS /@ ss));         (* <0| prod_{s in ss} o_s *)\nPvec[ss_List] := Flatten[KroneckerProduct @@ Table[facS[s, If[MemberQ[ss, s], 1, 0]], {s, 4}]];    (* P_e with support ss *)\nchecks[\"exchange dressing, same-type pairs (exact): P_{13} = [(th13-h) o1 o3 + h]/th13 and P_{24} = [(th24-h) o2 o4 + h]/th24 on <0|, also with the middle sites present: P_{123} = [(th13-h) o1o2o3 + h o2]/th13, P_{234} = [(th24-h) o2o3o4 + h o3]/th24\"] =\n  {Pvec[{1, 3}] === ((th[[1, 3]] - hN) oword[{1, 3}] + hN oword[{}])/th[[1, 3]], Pvec[{2, 4}] === ((th[[2, 4]] - hN) oword[{2, 4}] + hN oword[{}])/th[[2, 4]],\n   Pvec[{1, 2, 3}] === ((th[[1, 3]] - hN) oword[{1, 2, 3}] + hN oword[{2}])/th[[1, 3]], Pvec[{2, 3, 4}] === ((th[[2, 4]] - hN) oword[{2, 3, 4}] + hN oword[{3}])/th[[2, 4]]};\nchecks[\"adjacent pairs have no interference (exact): P_{12} = o1 o2, P_{23} = o2 o3, P_{34} = o3 o4\"] = {Pvec[{1, 2}] === oword[{1, 2}], Pvec[{2, 3}] === oword[{2, 3}], Pvec[{3, 4}] === oword[{3, 4}]};\n(* the two end sites: <0|o1 o4 = P_{14} + mu Q14 with Q14 = <S_14| rho_4(gamma^-1) (x) vac_2 (x) vac_3 and mu = -h/((th14 - 4h) det G) *)\nQ14 = Flatten[Transpose[ArrayReshape[Flatten[KroneckerProduct[Flatten[Inverse[GcN]], e4v, e1v]], {4, 4, 4, 4}], {1, 4, 2, 3}]];\nmu14 = -hN/((th[[1, 4]] - 4 hN) Det[GcN]);\nchecks[\"<0|o1 o4 = P_{14} + mu Q14, mu = -h/((th14 - 4h) det G), Q14 = <S_14|rho_4(gamma^-1) (x) e4^T (x) e1^T on sites (1,4),(2),(3) (exact)\"] = oword[{1, 4}] === Pvec[{1, 4}] + mu14 Q14;\n(* overlaps on all 256 eigenkets *)\novlOfC[w_] := N[w, $wp] . N[Rfr, $wp] . rAll;\nohat = Table[tauO[s]/lamS[s], {s, 4}];\nks = {2/7, -3/5, 4/9, 5/11};\nfamVec[kv_] := Flatten[KroneckerProduct @@ Table[vacOf1[s] . (id4 - kv[[s]] siteMat[chainData[\"L4\"][\"reps\"][[s]], MatrixPower[gam, pS[s]]]), {s, 4}]];\nA1 = 1 - ks[[1]] ohat[[1]]; B2 = 1 - ks[[2]] ohat[[2]]; C3 = 1 - ks[[3]] ohat[[3]]; D4 = 1 - ks[[4]] ohat[[4]];\npred123 = (A1 B2 C3 - (hN/th[[1, 3]]) ks[[1]] ks[[3]] (ohat[[1]] ohat[[3]] - 1) B2) ov0;\npred234 = (B2 C3 D4 - (hN/th[[2, 4]]) ks[[2]] ks[[4]] (ohat[[2]] ohat[[4]] - 1) C3) ov0;\nchecks[\"overlap <v1(k1) (x) v2(k2) (x) v3(k3) (x) vac_4|Psi_n> = [A B C - (h/th13) k1 k3 (ohat1 ohat3 - 1) B] <0|Psi_n>, A = 1 - k1 ohat1, B = 1 - k2 ohat2, C = 1 - k3 ohat3: max rel dev over 256 kets\"] = N[Max[Abs[ovlOfC[famVec[{ks[[1]], ks[[2]], ks[[3]], 0}]] - pred123]/Abs[ov0]], 3];\nchecks[\"overlap <vac_1 (x) v2 (x) v3 (x) v4|Psi_n> = [B C D - (h/th24) k2 k4 (ohat2 ohat4 - 1) C] <0|Psi_n>: max rel dev\"] = N[Max[Abs[ovlOfC[famVec[{0, ks[[2]], ks[[3]], ks[[4]]}]] - pred234]/Abs[ov0]], 3];\nchecks[\"adjacent two-site families: <v1 (x) v2 (x) vac|Psi_n> = A B <0|Psi_n> and <vac (x) v2 (x) v3 (x) vac|Psi_n> = B C <0|Psi_n>: max rel dev\"] = N[{Max[Abs[ovlOfC[famVec[{ks[[1]], ks[[2]], 0, 0}]] - A1 B2 ov0]/Abs[ov0]], Max[Abs[ovlOfC[famVec[{0, ks[[2]], ks[[3]], 0}]] - B2 C3 ov0]/Abs[ov0]]}, 3];\nchecks[\"all four sites (ends interfere): <v1 (x) .. (x) v4|Psi_n> / <0|Psi_n> - A B C D: nonzero, relative size (max over kets)\"] = N[Max[Abs[ovlOfC[famVec[ks]] - A1 B2 C3 D4 ov0]/Abs[ov0]], 3];\nGrid[Transpose[{Keys[checks][[n0 + 1 ;;]], Values[checks][[n0 + 1 ;;]]}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Results, cell 29:** **(exact) exchange dressing:** on <0|, **P_13 = [(th13-h) o1 o3 + h]/th13, P_24 = [(th24-h) o2 o4 + h]/th24, P_123 = [(th13-h) o1 o2 o3 + h o2]/th13, P_234 = [(th24-h) o2 o3 o4 + h o3]/th24**; adjacent products have no interference, P_12 = o1 o2, P_23 = o2 o3, P_34 = o3 o4. **The end pair (exact): <0|o1 o4 = P_14 + mu Q14, mu = -h/((th14 - 4h) det G), Q14 = <S_14|rho_4(gamma^-1) (x) e4^T (x) e1^T** (singlet-channel covector on sites 1,4): the two end sites do NOT factorise; **so (c) is answered NEGATIVELY: the plain product (1 - kappa o1)(1 - kappa o4) is not the product covector v1 (x) vac (x) vac (x) v4; the deviation is kappa1 kappa4 mu Q14.** **Overlap polynomials [numeric 60 digits, max rel dev 10^-51..10^-53 over 256 eigenkets]**, A = 1 - k1 ohat1, B = 1 - k2 ohat2, C = 1 - k3 ohat3, D = 1 - k4 ohat4: **<v1(k1) (x) v2(k2) (x) v3(k3) (x) vac_4|Psi> = [A B C - (h/th13) k1 k3 (ohat1 ohat3 - 1) B] <0|Psi>** and **<vac_1 (x) v2 (x) v3 (x) v4|Psi> = [B C D - (h/th24) k2 k4 (ohat2 ohat4 - 1) C] <0|Psi>**; the adjacent two-site families give A B and B C (10^-53). For all four kappa the naive product A B C D is NOT the overlap (the relative deviation is of order 54).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 2(b): block {1,2} on the SoV vacuum (g = 1). The four localising words <0|o1^x o2^y (x, y in {0,1}) have B-parts a_x (x) b_y with\n   a_0 = e1^T, a_1 = e1^T gamma (site 1), b_0 = e4^T, b_1 = e4^T G (site 2); no singlet term at g = 1 (e1^T . e3 = 0).\n   Hence the 4-dim span is the full 2 (x) 2 and its rank-1 elements form the Segre quadric c00 c11 = c01 c10: TWO free parameters (kappa_1, kappa_2). *)\nn0 = Length[checks];\na0 = e1v; a1 = e1v . gam; b0 = e4v; b1 = e4v . GcN;\nB12part[ss_List] := locParts[oword[ss], \"12\"];\nchecks[\"B-parts of the words <0|o1^x o2^y localise on block {1,2} (exact) and equal a_x (x) b_y\"] = Table[With[{r = B12part[Select[{1, 2}, {x, y}[[#]] == 1 &]]}, {x, y} -> (r[[1]] && r[[2]] === Flatten[KroneckerProduct[If[x == 1, a1, a0], If[y == 1, b1, b0]]])], {x, 0, 1}, {y, 0, 1}] // Flatten;\nchecks[\"a_0, a_1 linearly independent (rank), b_0, b_1 linearly independent (rank), pair-singlet overlaps a_x . b_y^T for (x,y) = (0,0),(0,1);(1,0),(1,1) [a_1 = -e4^T/c4, b_1 = e3^T]\"] = {MatrixRank[{a0, a1}], MatrixRank[{b0, b1}], Table[{a0, a1}[[x + 1]] . {b0, b1}[[y + 1]], {x, 0, 1}, {y, 0, 1}]};\n(* general element of the span: M = [a0;a1]^T C [b0;b1], rank M = rank C; rank-1 elements: C = x y^T *)\nCsym = {{c00, c01}, {c10, c11}};\nMsym = Transpose[{a0, a1}] . Csym . {b0, b1};\nchecks[\"rank of M(C) = rank of C (generic C): 2 x 2 minors of M vanish iff c00 c11 - c01 c10 = 0\"] = Union[Together /@ Flatten[Minors[Msym, 2]]] // Factor // Union;\n(* pure block rotations <0|rho_1(K) rho_2(K), K = u + v gamma: e4^T K^-T must lie in span{b0, b1} *)\nKsym = id4 + v gam;\nv2 = e4v . Transpose[Inverse[Ksym]] // Together;\nmins = Together /@ Flatten[Minors[{v2, b0, b1}, 3]];\nsolv = Quiet[Reduce[And @@ ((Numerator[#] == 0) & /@ DeleteCases[mins, 0]), v, Complexes]];\nchecks[\"pure block rotations of sites {1,2} inside the span: K = 1 + v gamma has e4^T K^-T in span{e4^T, e4^T G} only for v = (solution set)\"] = solv;\nchecks[\"the pure block rotation by gamma is the point at infinity (c00 = c01 = c10 = 0): <0|o1 o2 = <0|rho_1(gamma) rho_2(gamma) exactly (exact)\"] = oword[{1, 2}] === Flatten[KroneckerProduct[a1, b1, e1v, e4v]];\n(* parametrisation: v1 = a0 - k1 a1, v2 = b0 - k2 b1 -> c = (1, -k2, -k1, k1 k2) in the basis (00, 01, 10, 11) *)\nchecks[\"two-parameter family (exact, symbolic k1, k2): v1(k1) (x) v2(k2) (x) vac_34 = o-polynomial (1 - k1 o1)(1 - k2 o2) <0| = (1 - k1 o1 - k2 o2 + k1 k2 o1 o2) <0|\"] = Simplify[Flatten[KroneckerProduct[a0 - k1 a1, b0 - k2 b1, e1v, e4v]] - (oword[{}] - k1 oword[{1}] - k2 oword[{2}] + k1 k2 oword[{1, 2}])] === ConstantArray[0, 256];\nGrid[Transpose[{Keys[checks][[n0 + 1 ;;]], Values[checks][[n0 + 1 ;;]]}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Results, cell 31 (exact):** on block {1,2} at g = 1 the four words <0|o1^x o2^y have B-parts exactly a_x (x) b_y with a_0 = e1^T, a_1 = e1^T gamma = -e4^T/E4, b_0 = e4^T, b_1 = e4^T G = e3^T (both pairs linearly independent); the pair-singlet overlaps a_x.b_y^T are (0, 0; -7/5, 0), the one relevant for the word o1 o2 vanishes, so **there is no singlet obstruction at g = 1** (for generic g the site-2 word carries a singlet term). The span is the full 2 (x) 2; the 2 x 2 minors of the B-part of c00 <0| + c01 <0|o2 + c10 <0|o1 + c11 <0|o1 o2 vanish iff c00 c11 = c01 c10: **the product covectors form the Segre quadric with TWO free parameters**, v1(k1) (x) v2(k2) (x) vac_34 = (1 - k1 o1)(1 - k2 o2) <0| (exact, symbolic k1, k2). **Pure block rotations** <0|rho_1(K) rho_2(K), K = 1 + v gamma, lie in the span only for v = 0 (K = 1) and at infinity K ~ gamma, where <0|o1 o2 = <0|rho_1(gamma) rho_2(gamma) exactly: **the only pure block rotations are by 1 and by gamma = G^-T.** The singlet term cannot be cancelled by the two parameters (there is none to cancel at g = 1).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 2(c) continued: do larger pools of words reach the products that rotate both end sites?  Pools = all words X^a Y^b Z^c W^d with exponents in a window\n   (negative exponent = inverse operator). The 16 products P_e are tested for membership in the span of the pool (exact rank tests). *)\nn0 = Length[checks];\nopP[s_, k_] := If[k == 0, {}, If[k > 0, ConstantArray[opS[s], k], ConstantArray[Switch[s, 1, tD[1, thL4[[1]]], 4, tD[1, thL4[[4]]], _, tDi[1, thL4[[s]]]], -k]]];\nsubsE2 = Tuples[{0, 1}, 4];\nprodsP2 = Table[Flatten[KroneckerProduct @@ Table[facS[s, e[[s]]], {s, 4}]], {e, subsE2}];\npoolTest[rg_] := Module[{expsets = Tuples[rg, 4], vecs, rk}, vecs = Table[covW[OmC, Join @@ Table[opP[s, ex[[s]]], {s, 4}]], {ex, expsets}]; rk = MatrixRank[vecs];\n   {rg, Length[expsets], rk, StringJoin @@ (ToString /@ Boole[Table[MatrixRank[Append[vecs, prodsP2[[i]]]] == rk, {i, 16}]])}];\npoolRes = poolTest /@ {{0, 1}, {0, 1, 2}, {-1, 0, 1}, {-1, 0, 1, 2}};\nchecks[\"word pools (exponent windows): {window, number of words, rank, membership string for P_e, e = 0000, 0001, ..., 1111 in lexicographic order (1 = in the span)}\"] = poolRes;\nGrid[Transpose[{Keys[checks][[n0 + 1 ;;]], Values[checks][[n0 + 1 ;;]]}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Results, cell 33 (exact):** word pools X^a Y^b Z^c W^d with exponents in a window (negative exponent = inverse operator): windows {0,1} (16 words, rank 16), {0,1,2} (81 words, rank 81) and {-1,0,1} (81 words, rank 81) all contain exactly the products P_e with e not in {1001, 1011, 1101, 1111} (membership string 1111111110101010 over e = 0000..1111), i.e. **the products rotating both end sites are not reachable by words of these pools**; the window {-1,0,1,2} (256 words) spans the whole space (membership all 1), so the statement concerns word length, not reachability in principle.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 2(d): the omega-type parameters = the global torus rho(X), X in C[G^T], in the Bethe algebra; parameter count of the full family.\n   rho(X) = rho_A(X) (x) rho_F(X) (x) rho_A(X) (x) rho_F(X) = X (x) X^-T (x) X (x) X^-T. In the diagonal frame X = P^T diag(x) P^-T = f(G^T), f(z_i) = x_i, and rho(X) acts on an eigenket of weight w as prod_i x_i^{w_i}. *)\nn0 = Length[checks]; $wp = 60;\nXpoly[xs_] := Sum[xs[[k + 1]] MatrixPower[Transpose[GcN], k], {k, 0, 3}];\nrhoTot[Xm_] := KroneckerProduct[grpA[Xm], grpF[Xm], grpA[Xm], grpF[Xm]];\nxs0 = {2/3, -1/5, 3/4, 1/7}; X0 = Xpoly[xs0];\nxz = Table[Sum[xs0[[k + 1]] zN[[i]]^k, {k, 0, 3}], {i, 4}];     (* f(z_i): the eigenvalues of X *)\nchecks[\"X0 invertible; eigenvalues f(z_i) of X0 = f(G^T)\"] = {Det[X0] =!= 0, xz};\nchecks[\"rho(X0) commutes with t_a(u) exactly in the companion frame (a = 1, 2; u = 1/5)\"] = And @@ Table[With[{t = Normal[tA[\"L4\", GcN, a, 1/5]]}, rhoTot[X0] . t === t . rhoTot[X0]], {a, 2}];\nXbad = {{1, 2, 0, 1}, {0, 1, 3, 1}, {2, 0, 1, 1}, {1, 1, 1, 2}};\nchecks[\"for a generic X not in C[G^T] the commutator does not vanish (a = 1)\"] = With[{t = Normal[tA[\"L4\", GcN, 1, 1/5]]}, rhoTot[Xbad] . t =!= t . rhoTot[Xbad]];\nrhoDiag = DiagonalMatrix[Table[Times @@ (xz^wtOf[s]), {s, 256}]];\nchecks[\"rho(X0) = R diag(prod_i x_i^{w_i}) R^-1 exactly (R = rho(P^T), weights w of the product basis)\"] = rhoTot[X0] === Rfr . rhoDiag . Rfri;\n(* eigenvalue of rho(X0) on the 256 eigenkets from the weight blocks: w = weight of the block *)\nwOfEig = Table[wtOf[wBlocks[[blockOf[[n]]]][[1]]], {n, 256}];\nevPred = Table[N[Times @@ (xz^wOfEig[[n]]), $wp], {n, 256}];\novlOf[w_] := N[w, $wp] . N[Rfr, $wp] . rAll;\nov0 = ovlOf[OmC];\nchecks[\"<0|rho(X0)|Psi_n> = prod_i x_i^{w_i(n)} <0|Psi_n> on all 256 eigenkets: max rel dev\"] = N[Max[Abs[ovlOf[OmC . rhoTot[X0]] - evPred ov0]/Abs[ov0]], 3];\nchecks[\"number of distinct torus eigenvalue functions (distinct weights among the 256 eigenkets)\"] = Length[Union[wOfEig]];\n(* parameter count: map (x_0..x_3, kappa_1..kappa_4) -> covector <0| rho(X) (x)_s (1 - kappa_s rho_s(gamma^{p_s})), Jacobian rank at a random rational point *)\ncovF[xs_, ks_] := Module[{Xm = Xpoly[xs], Xit}, Xit = Transpose[Inverse[Xm]];\n   Flatten[KroneckerProduct[e1v . (id4 - ks[[1]] gam) . Xm, e4v . (id4 - ks[[2]] GcN) . Xit, e1v . (id4 - ks[[3]] Transpose[GcN]) . Xm, e4v . (id4 - ks[[4]] Inverse[GcN]) . Xit]]];\npt0 = {xs0, {1/3, -2/5, 3/7, 5/9}};\nchecks[\"covF reproduces <0| at X = 1, kappa = 0; and the site-vector form of cell 9\"] = {covF[{1, 0, 0, 0}, {0, 0, 0, 0}] === OmC, covF[{1, 0, 0, 0}, {3/7, 0, 0, 0}] === Flatten[KroneckerProduct[e1v . (id4 - 3/7 gam), e4v, e1v, e4v]]};\njac[idx_] := Table[Module[{xs = pt0[[1]], ks = pt0[[2]], sym = Unique[\"pp\"], f},\n     If[i <= 4, xs = ReplacePart[xs, i -> sym], ks = ReplacePart[ks, i - 4 -> sym]];\n     f = covF[xs, ks]; D[f, sym] /. sym -> If[i <= 4, pt0[[1, i]], pt0[[2, i - 4]]]], {i, idx}];\nv0 = covF @@ pt0;\nrankFull = MatrixRank[Prepend[jac[Range[8]], v0]] - 1;\nrankKap = MatrixRank[Prepend[jac[Range[5, 8]], v0]] - 1;\nrankX = MatrixRank[Prepend[jac[Range[1, 4]], v0]] - 1;\nchecks[\"projective dimension of the family: all 8 parameters (x_0..x_3, kappa_1..kappa_4), the four kappa only, the torus x only (rank of {v, dv/dp_i} minus 1)\"] = {rankFull, rankKap, rankX};\nGrid[Transpose[{Keys[checks][[n0 + 1 ;;]], Values[checks][[n0 + 1 ;;]]}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Results, cell 35:** **(d) the omega-type parameters.** For X in C[G^T] (X = x0 + x1 G^T + x2 G^2T + x3 G^3T, eigenvalues x_i = f(z_i) = sum_k x_k z_i^k), **rho(X) = X (x) X^-T (x) X (x) X^-T commutes exactly with t_a(u) in the companion frame** (a = 1, 2; the commutator is nonzero for a generic X outside C[G^T]), **rho(X) = R diag(prod_i x_i^{w_i}) R^-1 exactly**, and <0|rho(X)|Psi_n> = prod_i f(z_i)^{w_i(n)} <0|Psi_n> on all 256 eigenkets (max rel dev 10^-50, 55 distinct weight functions); so rho(X) is a (simple-spectrum) Bethe-algebra element and the global torus is the 4-parameter group of rho(X), one of whose parameters (overall scale of X) acts trivially on A F A F. **Parameter count [exact Jacobian at a random rational point]:** the map (x0..x3, k1..k4) -> <0| rho(X) (x)_s (1 - k_s rho_s(gamma^p_s)) has projective dimension **7 = 4 (kappa) + 3 (torus)** (the kappa alone 4, the torus alone 3).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Task 3: reach of the families (untwisted gl(4) projectors, exact)",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 3: reach of the families inside the 256-dim space, weight space by weight space and irrep by irrep of the UNTWISTED gl(4) action.\n   (1+15) (x) (1+15) = 2 (1) + 4 (15) + 20p + 45 + 45bar + 84.  Exact rational ranks; no epsilon anywhere. *)\nn0 = Length[checks]; SeedRandom[11];\nEsp[i_, j_] := Esp[i, j] = Sum[siteOp[\"L4\", s, chainData[\"L4\"][\"reps\"][[s]][i, j]], {s, 4}];\nC2 = Sum[Esp[i, j] . Esp[j, i], {i, 4}, {j, 4}]; C3 = Sum[Esp[i, j] . Esp[j, k] . Esp[k, i], {i, 4}, {j, 4}, {k, 4}];\nchecks[\"Casimirs C2, C3 symmetric and commute with every E_ij (exact)\"] = And @@ Flatten[Table[Normal[C2 . Esp[i, j] - Esp[i, j] . C2] === ConstantArray[0, {256, 256}] && Normal[C3 . Esp[i, j] - Esp[i, j] . C3] === ConstantArray[0, {256, 256}], {i, 4}, {j, 4}]] && Normal[C2] === Transpose[Normal[C2]] && Normal[C3] === Transpose[Normal[C3]];\ncmb = Normal[C2 + 7/13 C3];\nevsN = Eigenvalues[N[cmb]];\nclusters = Mean /@ GatherBy[Sort[evsN], Round[#, 10^-6] &];\nisoData = Table[Module[{vr = Rationalize[cl, 10^-8], B, d, P, hw, c2v}, B = NullSpace[cmb - vr IdentityMatrix[256]]; d = Length[B];\n    P = Transpose[B] . Inverse[B . Transpose[B]] . B;\n    hw = NullSpace[Join[Normal[Esp[1, 2]] . Transpose[B], Normal[Esp[2, 3]] . Transpose[B], Normal[Esp[3, 4]] . Transpose[B]]];\n    c2v = (B[[1]] . Normal[C2] . B[[1]])/(B[[1]] . B[[1]]);\n    {vr, d, P, Length[hw], Table[With[{v = Flatten[hw[[k]] . B]}, Table[(v . Normal[Esp[i, i]] . v)/(v . v), {i, 4}]], {k, Length[hw]}], c2v}], {cl, clusters}];\nirrDim[lam_] := Times @@ Flatten[Table[(lam[[i]] - lam[[j]] + j - i)/(j - i), {i, 4}, {j, i + 1, 4}]];\nisoTab = Table[{d[[1]], d[[2]], d[[4]], d[[5]], If[d[[4]] > 0, irrDim /@ d[[5]], {}]}, {d, isoData}];\nchecks[\"isotypic components of the untwisted action: {combined Casimir value, dimension of the isotypic subspace, multiplicity (number of highest-weight vectors), their gl(4) weights, irrep dimensions}\"] = isoTab;\nExport[FileNameJoin[{$TemporaryDirectory, \"ffbar-isoTab.m\"}], isoTab];\nPm = isoData[[All, 3]];\nrankIn[F_, P_] := MatrixRank[F . P];\nrandG[] := Module[{g}, While[Det[g = RandomInteger[{-2, 2}, {4, 4}]] == 0]; g];\nfamGlobal = Table[OmOf[\"L4\", randG[]], {130}];\nrandX[] := Module[{xs}, While[Det[Xpoly[xs = RandomInteger[{-4, 4}, 4]]] == 0]; xs];\nfamTorus = Table[OmC . rhoTot[Xpoly[randX[]]], {70}];\nfamKap = Table[covF[{1, 0, 0, 0}, RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, 4]], {40}];\nfamKapTor = Table[covF[randX[], RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, 4]], {330}];\nfamKap3 = Join[Table[covF[{1, 0, 0, 0}, Flatten[{RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, 3], 0}]], {12}], Table[covF[{1, 0, 0, 0}, Flatten[{0, RandomInteger[{-3, 3}, 3]}]], {12}]];\nfamKapGl = Flatten[Table[Module[{g = randG[]}, (# . rhoTot[g]) & /@ famKap[[1 ;; 6]]], {60}], 1];\nfams = <|\"global rotations <0|rho(g)\" -> famGlobal, \"global torus <0|rho(X), X in C[G^T]\" -> famTorus, \"kappa products, X = 1 (16-dim span)\" -> famKap, \"kappa products on the site sets {1,2,3} and {2,3,4}\" -> famKap3, \"kappa products + torus\" -> famKapTor, \"gl(4)-module generated by the kappa products (random g)\" -> famKapGl|>;\nreach = Table[{k, MatrixRank[fams[k]], Table[rankIn[fams[k], Pm[[i]]], {i, Length[Pm]}]}, {k, Keys[fams]}];\nchecks[\"reach: {family, rank in 256, projected rank into each isotypic component (order as in the isotypic table)}\"] = reach;\n(* minimal families: span of the products P_e with support in a given site set S (2^|S| covectors), projected rank per isotypic component *)\nPvecS[ss_List] := Flatten[KroneckerProduct @@ Table[facS[s, If[MemberQ[ss, s], 1, 0]], {s, 4}]];\nsiteSets = {{1}, {2}, {1, 2}, {2, 3}, {1, 3}, {1, 4}, {1, 2, 3}, {2, 3, 4}, {1, 2, 4}, {1, 2, 3, 4}};\nreachS = Table[Module[{fam = Table[PvecS[sub], {sub, Subsets[S]}]}, {S, MatrixRank[fam], Table[rankIn[fam, Pm[[i]]], {i, Length[Pm]}]}], {S, siteSets}];\nchecks[\"products P_e with support in the site set S (2^|S| covectors): {S, rank, projected rank into each isotypic component}\"] = reachS;\nreachW = Table[{k, Table[MatrixRank[fams[k][[All, blk]]], {blk, wBlocks}]}, {k, Keys[fams]}];\nchecks[\"total of the per-weight-space ranks per family (weight spaces of the untwisted action: 55 blocks, sizes 28, 12 x 12, 12 x 1, 24 x 2, 6 x 4)\"] = Table[{r[[1]], Total[r[[2]]]}, {r, reachW}];\nExport[FileNameJoin[{$TemporaryDirectory, \"ffbar-reach.m\"}], {reach, reachS, Length /@ wBlocks}];\nGrid[Transpose[{Keys[checks][[n0 + 1 ;;]], Values[checks][[n0 + 1 ;;]]}], Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Results, cell 38 (exact ranks; in each triple/list the order is: singlet (dimension 2 = 2 copies), 15 (60 = 4 copies), 45bar (HW (1,1,0,-2), 45), 20p (HW (1,1,-1,-1), 20), 84 (HW (2,0,0,-2)), 45 (HW (2,0,-1,-1), 45)):** the untwisted Casimirs C2, C3 commute with all E_ij and C2 + 7/13 C3 separates the six irrep types (values 0, 216/13, 264/13, 324/13, 540/13, 600/13); the isotypic dimensions 2, 60, 45, 20, 84, 45 and multiplicities 2, 4, 1, 1, 1, 1 are as expected from (1+15)(x)(1+15) = 2.1 + 4.15 + 20p + 45 + 45bar + 84 (exact). **Global family alone:** the rotations <0|rho(g) span the 84-dim top irrep (rank 84, projections (0,0,0,0,84,0)) and the global torus <0|rho(X) gives rank 55 inside it: **blind to every non-top irrep**. **The kappa products (the 16 covectors P_e):** rank 16 with projected ranks (1, 10, 12, 8, 16, 12): **all six irrep types become visible**, including the singlet (rank 1) and the 15. Single sites: site 1 (0,1,1,0,2,0) (15, 45bar, 84), site 2 (0,0,0,0,2,1) (84, 45); pairs {1,2}: (0,2,2,1,4,2), {2,3}: (0,0,2,1,4,2), {1,3}: (0,2,3,0,4,0), end pair {1,4}: (1,3,2,1,4,2); triples {1,2,3}: (0,4,6,3,8,4), {2,3,4}: (0,4,4,3,8,6), {1,2,4}: (1,6,4,3,8,6). **The singlet is seen only by products that rotate both end sites (those that are NOT polynomials in the words); the 12-dim span of the word-reachable products on {1,2,3} and {2,3,4} sees the 15, 45bar, 20p, 84, 45 with ranks (7, 8, 4, 12, 8) but not the singlet.** With the torus (330 random samples, rank 193): (1, 44, 45, 20, 84, 45); the gl(4)-module generated by the kappa products has dimension 240 = 256 - 16 with projections (1, 45, 45, 20, 84, 45): **only one copy of the singlet and three of the four copies of the 15 are ever seen; 45bar, 20p, 84, 45 completely.** Weight spaces: the global families have per-weight-space ranks 6 (zero-weight space of dimension 28), 3 (the twelve 12-dim spaces), 1 (the rest), 84 in total; the kappa + torus family and the module have per-weight-space ranks summing to 240.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Task 4 (stretch) and summary",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Summary (finite generic twist, g = 1, companion twist; NO untwisting / epsilon)\n\n| # | Claim | Status | Cell |\n|---|-------|--------|------|\n| 0a | gl(4) relations, S invariant, chains L4/B12/B34, Omega(g) = Omega_B12 (x) Omega_B34 | [exact] | 3 |\n| 0b | qdet closed form, commutativity, 55 weight blocks, frame relation t(comp) = R t(diag) R^-1 | [exact] | 5 |\n| 0c | twisted eigenbasis, simple spectrum, tau_a interpolation | [numeric 60 digits] | 7 |\n| L3 | <0|t1(th1)^-1 = c1 <0|rho_1(gamma), <0|t1(th4)^-1 = c4 <0|rho_4(gamma^-1), also for gX | [exact] | 10 |\n| L2 | singles localising on end blocks (t3(th1-h), t1(th1)^-1, t1(th2), t3(th4+3h), t1(th4)^-1, t1(th3)); the others do not; **at g = 1 t1(th2), t1(th3) rotate the interior sites alone** (no singlet) | [exact] | 12 |\n| L2b | t1(th_a) t3(th_a + m h) scalar at (a,m) = (1,-1),(2,3),(3,-1),(4,3); q1 closed form; so t3(th1-h) = q1 t1(th1)^-1 | [exact] | 10, 20 |\n| L1 | SoV words (a,k) localise on {1,2} (as the L=2 words (x) Omega_2) only for a in {0,3}, k in {0,1}; c_01 = th23 (th24-h), c_30 = prod_j (th13 - j h)(th14-h)(th14-2h)(th14-4h), c_31 = c_30 c_01 | [exact] | 12, 20 |\n| 1a | one-site constants c1, l2, l3, c4 in closed form; the 16 products X^e1 Y^e2 Z^e3 W^e4 are pure rotations iff e is a single site or an adjacent pair | [exact] | 20 |\n| 1b | exchange-dressed t1(th1) on {1,3}, t1(th4) on {2,4}; explicit single-site covectors | [exact] | 22 |\n| 1c | fused T_lambda scan: 2288 operators, 86 localise, 7 distinct classes; **no operator acts as gamma^p with abs(p) >= 2** | [numeric 60 digits] | 14, 16, 18 |\n| 2a | kappa-family <0|(1 - kappa t3(th1-h)/(q1 c1)) = e1^T(1 - kappa G^-T) (x) e4^T (x) e1^T (x) e4^T; overlap (1 - kappa ohat_1) <0|Psi> | [exact] / [numeric 60 digits] | 25 |\n| 2a2 | the same for sites 2, 3, 4 with group elements g2 = (1-kG)^-T, g3 = 1 - kG^T, g4 = (1-kG^-1)^-T | [exact] / [numeric] | 25 |\n| 2b | block {1,2}: B-parts a_x (x) b_y, no singlet obstruction at g = 1, rank-1 locus c00 c11 = c01 c10: 2 free parameters; pure block rotations only by 1, gamma | [exact] | 31 |\n| 2b2 | products of kappa-deformations that are polynomials in the words: maximal sets {1,2,3}, {2,3,4}; exchange expansions | [exact] | 27, 29 |\n| 2c | both end sites: does NOT factorise, <0|o1 o4 = P_14 + mu Q14 | [exact] | 29 |\n| 2d | global torus rho(X), X in C[G^T], in the Bethe algebra, eigenvalue prod f(z_i)^{w_i}; 7 free parameters (4 kappa + 3 torus) | [exact] / [numeric] | 35 |\n| 3 | reach: global family blind to non-top irreps; kappa products see all six irrep types; module = 240 of 256 | [exact] | 38 |\n| 4 | Q-form: only tau_3(th1-h) tau_1(th1) = q1 (so ohat_1 = h th12(th13+h)th14/tau_1(th1)); gl(4) Q-functions and the L = 4 SoV expansion NOT done | partial | 25 |\n\n**Explicit free-parameter families (all on <0| = e1^T (x) e4^T (x) e1^T (x) e4^T, twist G = G_c(z), gamma = G^-T, E_k = e_k(z)).**\nSite vectors (covectors): v1(k) = e1^T(1 - k G^-T) = (1, 0, 0, k/E4); v2(k) = e4^T(1 - k G) = (0, 0, -k, 1); v3(k) = e1^T(1 - k G^T) = (1 - k E1, -k, 0, 0); v4(k) = e4^T(1 - k G^-1) = (k/E4, -k E1/E4, k E2/E4, 1 - k E3/E4). Group elements: **site 1: g_1 = 1 - k1 G^-T; site 2: g_2 = (1 - k2 G)^-T; site 3: g_3 = 1 - k3 G^T; site 4: g_4 = (1 - k4 G^-1)^-T** (rho_A(g) = g, rho_F(g) = g^-T); with the global torus X = x0 + x1 G^T + x2 (G^T)^2 + x3 (G^T)^3 the covector is **<0|rho(X) (x)_s rho_s(g_s(k_s)) = (e1^T(1 - k1 G^-T) X) (x) (e4^T(1 - k2 G) X^-T) (x) (e1^T(1 - k3 G^T) X) (x) (e4^T(1 - k4 G^-1) X^-T)** (X commutes with all the g_s). The Bethe-algebra operators: o1 = t1(th1)^-1/c1 = t3(th1-h)/(q1 c1), o2 = t1(th2)/l2, o3 = t1(th3)/l3, o4 = t1(th4)^-1/c4, with <0|o_s = <0|rho_s(gamma^p_s), p = (1, 1, -1, -1). **Overlap formulas** (ohat_s = eigenvalue of o_s on Psi, <0|Psi> = the SoV-vacuum wave function; the torus contributes the factor prod_i f(z_i)^{w_i(Psi)}): one site, (1 - k_s ohat_s); sites {1,2}, {2,3}, {3,4}: (1 - k_a ohat_a)(1 - k_b ohat_b); **{1,2,3}: [A B C - (h/th13) k1 k3 (ohat1 ohat3 - 1) B]; {2,3,4}: [B C D - (h/th24) k2 k4 (ohat2 ohat4 - 1) C]; {1,3}: A C - (h/th13) k1 k3 (ohat1 ohat3 - 1); {2,4}: B D - (h/th24) k2 k4 (ohat2 ohat4 - 1)**, each times <0|Psi> (A, B, C, D = 1 - k_s ohat_s). With both end sites deformed the covector is [polynomial in the words] plus a singlet-channel term k1 k4 mu Q14-type, not a polynomial in the commuting operators within the pools tried.\n\n**Parameter count and reach.** 7 free projective parameters (4 kappa + 3 torus) as covectors; 6 of them (three consecutive kappa and the torus) have overlaps that are explicit polynomials in the transfer-matrix eigenvalues times <0|Psi>; the plain product of both end deformations picks up the singlet-channel term. Every site is only rotated inside the 2-plane span{vac_s, vac_s gamma^(+-1)}; relative rotations between sites of the same type (1,3 or 2,4) are polynomials in G^(+-T) with the exchange dressing above. Irrep reach: see cell 38: global rotations see only the 84; the 16 kappa products see all six irrep types (the singlet only through products rotating both ends); the generated gl(4)-module has dimension 240 (one singlet and one 15 copy missing).\n\n**Localising operators acting as a higher power of the twist on one site: none** in the scan (|lambda| <= 6, m = -5..5); all localising operators on at most 2 sites act as gamma^(+-1) (cell 18).\n\n**Surprises / flags.** (1) At g = 1 the singlet term of t1(theta2) (and t1(theta3)) vanishes: the interior sites 2 and 3 are rotated by single transfer matrices, contrary to the generic-g picture of the previous notebook. (2) The two ends cannot be rotated independently by the transfer-matrix words: the interference term is the singlet-channel covector mu Q14. (3) t3(th1-h), t3(th2+3h), t3(th3-h), t3(th4+3h) are exact qdet multiples of the inverse t1s (so the kappa family is the t1(th1)^-1 family); fused T_(2,1,1,1)(theta-h) are the same. (4) The main-session (L1) is confirmed with closed-form constants; (L2)/(L3) confirmed. (5) 60-digit numerics are used only for eigenstate overlaps and the fused-transfer-matrix scan; every identity on covectors is exact. (6) Not done: gl(4) Q-functions (Task 4 beyond tau_3 tau_1 = q1), the L = 4 SoV basis and the expansion support of the kappa covectors in it.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  }
 ],
 "metadata": {}
}